{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475607-m20-sorcerer-s-is-being-made","id":1475607,"title":"M20 Sorcerer's. Is being made","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-28T17:02:45-08:00","id":1475607,"title":"M20 Sorcerer's. Is being made","content":"According to the last mmn of This month","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T18:28:55-08:00","id":1475614,"title":"","content":"Sounds good to me. I hope for rules for playing non-Mage magicians, enlightened tech types, and psychics. A bunch of mystic non-Mage groups would be sweet too. Crossover rules for other splats would be useful. Mages can quickly get to a scale that just doesn't gel with Vamps, Wraiths, Werebeasts, Changelings, Mummies, et al. Since Mages are humans embracing the spark of divinity within all humans, their attaining godlike power (and the risks there in) fits their archetype. Having optional rules to supercharge Sorcerers to be more nearly equal to the major splats would make for easier crossover games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 02-28-2022, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T19:12:49-08:00","id":1475616,"title":"","content":"Ack! It's already in Art Direction? That was fast!<br /> <br /> Pure speculation here, brought on by the abruptness of this: is it possible that Onyx Path is trying another experiment, and that M20 sorcerer is in fact a revision of the STV supplement sorcerer: Paths of power? It would explain why it has jumped over so many of the usual steps; all that would be needed would be a review to ensure that all of the content meets the standards of an official book, plus some artwork to pretty it up, and then rerelease it as an official book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-28-2022, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-28T22:39:47-08:00","id":1475624,"title":"","content":"This I suspect is one of the books that had been progressing through the development pipeline for a while, it's only just now that OPP finally got the go ahead to properly announce it...<br /> <br /> ...well, ish. I pointedly noticed that unlike all of the other MMN 2022 updates, the M20 Sorcerer entry doesn't have any dev notes. And can't think of any reason why PDX would pump the brakes on OPP announcing this particular project.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T00:51:52-08:00","id":1475627,"title":"","content":"Wondering if it is art direction for a Kickstarter, rather than the full thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T02:17:19-08:00","id":1475629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475607-m20-sorcerer-s-is-being-made?p=1475616#post1475616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ack! It's already in Art Direction? That was fast!<br /> <br /> Pure speculation here, brought on by the abruptness of this: is it possible that Onyx Path is trying another experiment, and that M20 sorcerer is in fact a revision of the STV supplement sorcerer: Paths of power? It would explain why it has jumped over so many of the usual steps; all that would be needed would be a review to ensure that all of the content meets the standards of an official book, plus some artwork to pretty it up, and then rerelease it as an official book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps, though I would have thought Charles would have said something even if only that he couldn't say anything.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer: PoP covers all the bases and more already so I'm not sure what else they could put in an official book anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T07:58:53-08:00","id":1475637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>babi_gog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475607-m20-sorcerer-s-is-being-made?p=1475627#post1475627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wondering if it is art direction for a Kickstarter, rather than the full thing</div> </div> </div> </div>That I suspect not, since usually a book that\u2019s going to KS is marked as such as soon as it enters Art Direction. Which this book has not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T08:07:38-08:00","id":1475638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475607-m20-sorcerer-s-is-being-made?p=1475629#post1475629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps, though I would have thought Charles would have said something even if only that he couldn't say anything.<br /> <br /> Sorcerer: PoP covers all the bases and more already so I'm not sure what else they could put in an official book anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumes that anyone has asked Charles about it. Has anyone?<br /> <br /> And the only things I can think of that an official book would do that PoP didn't would be the official stamp of approval, and artwork. The former would involve going through the text to remove anything that would be okay for a fanon book but not for an official book; and the latter\u2026 well, that's where the Art Direction comes in.<br /> <br /> Again, I must stress that this is pure speculation. It would be an unusual move on onyx paths part to do that; and thus far, there is no evidence that that is indeed what they're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-01-2022, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T08:48:59-08:00","id":1475641,"title":"","content":"If that is what's happening, I think that it's a good thing, with one caveat. The upsides are that Onyx path is getting another official mage supplement \u201con the cheap\u201d, in that all of the writing has already been done, and has even been given a couple of editorial passes \u2014 albeit from freelance editors (so an official editorial pass would be a good thing). The benefits to Charles is that his book will end up getting better publicity. As nice as it is to be able to publish through storytellers vault, fans of the world of Darkness aren't even aware that it's a thing; and many who are tend to be dismissive of it. So getting and official step of approval through re-release as an official book can only help sales.<br /> <br /> The caveat is the question of what happens for those of us who purchased PoP. Personally, if M20 sorcerer is indeed just an officially edited PoP, I would hope that those of us who purchased PoP would get the official book as an update to our PoP purchase. I would actually have to think twice about purchasing a book that I have already bought once. I would probably end up fighting the bullets and doing so anyway; but I wouldn't be happy about it. <br /> <br /> If M20 sorcerer is <i>not</i> \u201cmerely\u201d an officially sanctioned version of PoP, either because it uses PoP as a baseline but makes significant changes or because it was developed independently of PoP, that's a whole other matter. As a purchaser of PoP, getting M20 Sorcerer will be lower on my priority list than usual; but in that case, I won't feel so bad about it. I might, however, feel a little bad for Charles, as one of the top sellers in the storytellers vault will have been taken out from under him. That said, that's one of the risks that one takes publishing Storyteller Vault material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T14:01:19-08:00","id":1475652,"title":"","content":"Well, I'll buy it anyway as I want them to keep making as many 20th books as possible for as long as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T14:22:38-08:00","id":1475653,"title":"","content":"I get that; and I even agree with it, to an extent. And back when my finances weren't quite so tight, I wouldn't hesitate to essentially repurchase something that I already own in order to keep M20 going. Unfortunately, I recently lost my job and have been struggling to keep my bills paid. So I have to be a lot more choosy about what I spend my money on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-09T05:37:50-08:00","id":1476090,"title":"","content":"This is great news! We finally need proper sorcery rules and magic compared to what we got in HH2, Kinfolk, and Ghost Hunter. If they do use Charles' PoP then that would be great, but I think they should also borrow some ideas from Falco's Sorcerer's Companion book which is also good!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T13:07:51-08:00","id":1476279,"title":"","content":"My thought about feeling bad for Charles if M20 Sorcerer <i>isn't</i> a revised PoP goes double for Falco if they end up borrowing material from his book that undercuts any new sales he might otherwise get. Though I suspect they won't; Onyx Path tends to be very considerate of the Storytellers Vault content creators. <br /> <br /> What I would consider to be a better solution would be for them <i>not</i> to borrow anything from Falco, and to let him release an updated version of his Sorcerer's Companion that is designed to work with the official M20 Sorcerer rather than Sorcerer Revised. That would largely involve ditching the M20 chapter from the existing supplement, which is almost exclusively about adapting SRev for use with M20; but I could see Falco expanding on the remaining chapters, too, building on what M20 Sorcerer introduces that SRev didn't have. <br /> <br /> As for S:PoP, if Onyx Path <i>is</i> using it as a baseline, the recently pre-released Operative's Dossier has something in it that I hope becomes a change in M20 Sorcerer: on SPoP pp.79\u201380, there are rules for mages creating sorcerous Paths. These are an adaptation of the Talisman creation rules found in the Book of Secrets. If mages creating Paths is a thing in M20 Sorcerer at all, I'd like to see it based off of the Terranorming process outlined in the Operative's Dossier rather than the Wonder creation rules. Conceptually, it strikes me as a better fit. <br /> <br /> Another thing I'd like to see M20 Sorcerer do differently than SPoP is the dice pools for the Paths. SPoP introduced the notion of basing a Path's dice pool off of the sorcerer's Practice, a move that I agree with in principle; but in practice, this resulted in all of the dice pools being changed to strip out any reference to specific Abilities. For example, SRev's Path of Alchemy lists the dice pool as \u201cIntelligence+Alchemy (Alchemical Procedures), Intelligence+Herbalism (Herbalism Procedures), Intelligence+Science (Advanced Chemistry Procedures)\u201d, while SPoP states it simply as \u201cIntelligence+Ability\u201d. For M20 Sorcerer, I'd like to see SPoP's Practice-based Abilities notion implemented, but with each Path write-up being given at least one example (\u201ccoincidentally\u201d aligning with the dice pools provided in the original material). The M20 Sorcerer write-up for Alchemy, for instance, might say something like \u201cIntelligence + Ability (e.g., Esoterica (Alchemy) for traditional alchemy, Pharmacopeia for herbalism, or Science (Chemistry) for advanced chemistry)\u201d. <br /> <br /> That said, I'd be inclined to replace the use of Occult in dice pools with Esoterica: the Occult Knowledge in M20 is described as \u201ca generalized comprehension of the mystical world <i>as most Sleepers understand it</i>\u201d that is \u201coften misleading, incomplete, or flat-out wrong\u201d. By explicit contrast, Esoterica \u201crepresents the <i>practical</i> application of unusual fields\u201d. I'd make an exception of the sorcerer's Practice is Gutter Magic, as the whole point of Gutter Magic is that its practitioners don't really know what they're doing, but somehow make it work anyway; though ironically, Occult isn't listed among Gutter Magic's Associated Abilities (something I'd tweak in M20 Sorcerer).<br /> <br /> I might also include a box somewhere talking about how HH2, Kinfolk, and Ghosts Hunters Hedge Magic relate to Sorcery, with the main takeaway being that in general, \u201cHedge Magic\u201d is a pejorative term used by sorcerers, who see it as Sorcery using the Practice of Gutter Magic. (It isn't, for what it's worth: in particular, the Path of Divination is wildly different in each of these books. Heck, Ghost Hunters classifies it as a Psychic Phenomenon rather than a Hedge Path.)<br /> <br /> And speaking of Practices, I'd love to see each Path include a \u201cCommon Practices\u201d entry that talks about good fits between Path and Practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T05:23:55-07:00","id":1476375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1475607-m20-sorcerer-s-is-being-made?p=1476279#post1476279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My thought about feeling bad for Charles if M20 Sorcerer <i>isn't</i> a revised PoP goes double for Falco if they end up borrowing material from his book that undercuts any new sales he might otherwise get. Though I suspect they won't; Onyx Path tends to be very considerate of the Storytellers Vault content creators.<br /> <br /> What I would consider to be a better solution would be for them <i>not</i> to borrow anything from Falco, and to let him release an updated version of his Sorcerer's Companion that is designed to work with the official M20 Sorcerer rather than Sorcerer Revised. That would largely involve ditching the M20 chapter from the existing supplement, which is almost exclusively about adapting SRev for use with M20; but I could see Falco expanding on the remaining chapters, too, building on what M20 Sorcerer introduces that SRev didn't have.<br /> <br /> As for S:PoP, if Onyx Path <i>is</i> using it as a baseline, the recently pre-released Operative's Dossier has something in it that I hope becomes a change in M20 Sorcerer: on SPoP pp.79\u201380, there are rules for mages creating sorcerous Paths. These are an adaptation of the Talisman creation rules found in the Book of Secrets. If mages creating Paths is a thing in M20 Sorcerer at all, I'd like to see it based off of the Terranorming process outlined in the Operative's Dossier rather than the Wonder creation rules. Conceptually, it strikes me as a better fit.<br /> <br /> Another thing I'd like to see M20 Sorcerer do differently than SPoP is the dice pools for the Paths. SPoP introduced the notion of basing a Path's dice pool off of the sorcerer's Practice, a move that I agree with in principle; but in practice, this resulted in all of the dice pools being changed to strip out any reference to specific Abilities. For example, SRev's Path of Alchemy lists the dice pool as \u201cIntelligence+Alchemy (Alchemical Procedures), Intelligence+Herbalism (Herbalism Procedures), Intelligence+Science (Advanced Chemistry Procedures)\u201d, while SPoP states it simply as \u201cIntelligence+Ability\u201d. For M20 Sorcerer, I'd like to see SPoP's Practice-based Abilities notion implemented, but with each Path write-up being given at least one example (\u201ccoincidentally\u201d aligning with the dice pools provided in the original material). The M20 Sorcerer write-up for Alchemy, for instance, might say something like \u201cIntelligence + Ability (e.g., Esoterica (Alchemy) for traditional alchemy, Pharmacopeia for herbalism, or Science (Chemistry) for advanced chemistry)\u201d.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be inclined to replace the use of Occult in dice pools with Esoterica: the Occult Knowledge in M20 is described as \u201ca generalized comprehension of the mystical world <i>as most Sleepers understand it</i>\u201d that is \u201coften misleading, incomplete, or flat-out wrong\u201d. By explicit contrast, Esoterica \u201crepresents the <i>practical</i> application of unusual fields\u201d. I'd make an exception of the sorcerer's Practice is Gutter Magic, as the whole point of Gutter Magic is that its practitioners don't really know what they're doing, but somehow make it work anyway; though ironically, Occult isn't listed among Gutter Magic's Associated Abilities (something I'd tweak in M20 Sorcerer).<br /> <br /> I might also include a box somewhere talking about how HH2, Kinfolk, and Ghosts Hunters Hedge Magic relate to Sorcery, with the main takeaway being that in general, \u201cHedge Magic\u201d is a pejorative term used by sorcerers, who see it as Sorcery using the Practice of Gutter Magic. (It isn't, for what it's worth: in particular, the Path of Divination is wildly different in each of these books. Heck, Ghost Hunters classifies it as a Psychic Phenomenon rather than a Hedge Path.)<br /> <br /> And speaking of Practices, I'd love to see each Path include a \u201cCommon Practices\u201d entry that talks about good fits between Path and Practice.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Excellent points! I hope your ideas get implemented in some fashion in M20: Sorcerer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}